(866444, 97522, 25203, '<td valign="top">Great Title. Looks a little soft.  When shooting through most glass AF will hit a few mm far from the subject.  I just chronicled a whole fish pet shop and also found that the scales stand out much better if you offset a KEY at 45 degrees to the fish. Remember that light will penetrate 2-3 MM into the fish before refracting.</td>', 'Great Title. Looks a little soft.  When shooting through most glass AF will hit a few mm far from the subject.  I just chronicled a whole fish pet shop and also found that the scales stand out much better if you offset a KEY at 45 degrees to the fish. Remember that light will penetrate 2-3 MM into the fish before refracting.', '2004-08-18 20:46:33.000000', NULL, 1),
