(876126, 98191, 24969, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for the comments and votes!<br/> <br/>This was shot through a window- it was twilight and I caught some reflection on the glass. When I turned the brightness down I lost the neon "glow", but it really clarified the image and gave it a nice depth. (but not on the red for whatever reason) Bumped up the individual color levels after that. Ended up cropping it twice- couldn''t quite find something I really liked and ended up going with the tight shot.<br/> <br/>Hoping to take more "natural" pics- my first few entries here have some heavy-handed adjustments in Elements. I''ll get there...<br/> <br/>Thanks again all. Your beautiful work is very inspiring and I''m learning something everytime I log in. What a great site! <br/></td>', 'Thanks to all for the comments and votes! This was shot through a window- it was twilight and I caught some reflection on the glass. When I turned the brightness down I lost the neon "glow", but it really clarified the image and gave it a nice depth. (but not on the red for whatever reason) Bumped up the individual color levels after that. Ended up cropping it twice- couldn''t quite find something I really liked and ended up going with the tight shot. Hoping to take more "natural" pics- my first few entries here have some heavy-handed adjustments in Elements. I''ll get there... Thanks again all. Your beautiful work is very inspiring and I''m learning something everytime I log in. What a great site! ', '2004-08-25 06:16:46.000000', NULL, 0),
