(876156, 98116, 25347, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the great positive feedback!  I had two goals going into my first challenge: A) A top half finish and B) top 50 finish.  I achieved A with room to spare (I was one place off from being in the top quarter), but by seven places missed out on B!  Ah well, c''est la vie.  This shot was taken at Coaster''s Drive-in Resteraunt at Cedar Point Amusement Part in Sandusky, Ohio at around 7:45 PM.  As much as I wanted a darker shot, I also equally wanted the detail on the car, and not to blend in with the rest of the submissions, which I assumed would be mostly and bright subject on a pitch black setting.  While it''s clear most people preferred the latter, I was still satisfied with this shot.  One other thing that has been suggested to me is to darken the picture in Photoshop, however I am a firm believer that a picture is best in its raw form.  No editing whatsoever (save for a crop of about 10 pixels to remove a wayward foot) was used in this photo, and that''s a fact I''m very proud of.  Thanks to everyone who voted, commented, or just viewed (especially bledford, who thought I did a better job even though the other picture is a few pages ahead of me and has boostering support on how it should''ve ribboned :) )<br/> <br/>-James</td>', 'Thanks all for the great positive feedback!  I had two goals going into my first challenge: A) A top half finish and B) top 50 finish.  I achieved A with room to spare (I was one place off from being in the top quarter), but by seven places missed out on B!  Ah well, c''est la vie.  This shot was taken at Coaster''s Drive-in Resteraunt at Cedar Point Amusement Part in Sandusky, Ohio at around 7:45 PM.  As much as I wanted a darker shot, I also equally wanted the detail on the car, and not to blend in with the rest of the submissions, which I assumed would be mostly and bright subject on a pitch black setting.  While it''s clear most people preferred the latter, I was still satisfied with this shot.  One other thing that has been suggested to me is to darken the picture in Photoshop, however I am a firm believer that a picture is best in its raw form.  No editing whatsoever (save for a crop of about 10 pixels to remove a wayward foot) was used in this photo, and that''s a fact I''m very proud of.  Thanks to everyone who voted, commented, or just viewed (especially bledford, who thought I did a better job even though the other picture is a few pages ahead of me and has boostering support on how it should''ve ribboned :) ) -James', '2004-08-25 07:18:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(876169, 98498, 25065, '<td valign="top">Congratz! Definitely going into my Favorites!</td>', 'Congratz! Definitely going into my Favorites!', '2004-08-25 07:36:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(876222, 98498, 4482, '<td valign="top">This is such a kewl shot! Congrats !!!</td>', 'This is such a kewl shot! Congrats !!!', '2004-08-25 08:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(876231, 98257, 11793, '<td valign="top">good shot - well done</td>', 'good shot - well done', '2004-08-25 08:20:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(876258, 97965, 23614, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for your votes and your comments. When I shot that picture I was experimenting and I was not going after this shot at all. I wanted some bright colors (even though I did not realized yet neon meant "bright colors" or "fluorescent" because in French, it''s only refering to the lamp. I only realized that when voting!!!). I finally thought of those long forgotten light bright pegs that were still in a box and waiting for my child to be old enough to play with. I''m glad it brought back some good memories to some of you!</td>', 'Thanks to all for your votes and your comments. When I shot that picture I was experimenting and I was not going after this shot at all. I wanted some bright colors (even though I did not realized yet neon meant "bright colors" or "fluorescent" because in French, it''s only refering to the lamp. I only realized that when voting!!!). I finally thought of those long forgotten light bright pegs that were still in a box and waiting for my child to be old enough to play with. I''m glad it brought back some good memories to some of you!', '2004-08-25 08:42:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(876264, 98498, 1368, '<td valign="top">about time you got a ribbon!<br/>Congrats great shot!</td>', 'about time you got a ribbon!Congrats great shot!', '2004-08-25 08:50:16.000000', NULL, 0),
