INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(884131, 97873, 17126, '<td valign="top">Man this thing is so awesome. Judging by the difference in avg vote from all users and the avg vote from just the commenters, it''s controversially an awesome piece! I think that''s way cooler than having a nice, balanced, predictable piece too which everyone is appealed. Nice job, and Iwould hang it on my wall! In fact, I think you shouldm ake prints available, I''d like a 36" x 48" if you don''t mind. :)</td>', 'Man this thing is so awesome. Judging by the difference in avg vote from all users and the avg vote from just the commenters, it''s controversially an awesome piece! I think that''s way cooler than having a nice, balanced, predictable piece too which everyone is appealed. Nice job, and Iwould hang it on my wall! In fact, I think you shouldm ake prints available, I''d like a 36" x 48" if you don''t mind. :)', '2004-08-30 14:46:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(884452, 98376, 16912, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in Neon but would probably have given it a 5 or 6. Now, don''t get me wrong but if I''d have known it was taken by a 12 year old it would probably have scored a 7 or 8 from me. Not only do you have talent behind the lens (composition etc) but you already have a fine grasp on post editing. I look forward to more of your pictures Andrea.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in Neon but would probably have given it a 5 or 6. Now, don''t get me wrong but if I''d have known it was taken by a 12 year old it would probably have scored a 7 or 8 from me. Not only do you have talent behind the lens (composition etc) but you already have a fine grasp on post editing. I look forward to more of your pictures Andrea.', '2004-08-30 18:57:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(884478, 98376, 25150, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7. <br/>You better stick with photography!!!!!<br/></td>', 'I gave this a 7. You better stick with photography!!!!!', '2004-08-30 19:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(884523, 98430, 22913, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Love it.<br/>Ross</td>', 'Congratulations, Love it.Ross', '2004-08-30 20:04:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(884735, 97873, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/> <br/>With this piece you have entered the controversial world of the love or hated image. Here we are not going to spend time duscussing composition but rather some of the procedures employed to produce these type of images. Since you as the creator is not even aware of the final shape of such creations it then behooves you to do many takes so that the most pleasing can be selected. It involves many takes and then closing the lens and changing the time. After some experience you will develop a taste for the most appropiate selection and the technique you wish to employ.<br/> <br/>The variations range from holding camera steady and then suddenly flipping upside down first with equal split of the time and then 2/3 time and then flipping, etc. Another idea is to use a black cardboard and cover half the lens and then either getting the cardbotd out of the way or covering the other half.<br/> <br/>Another idea is to hold camera steady and then zoom either in out out, both give you interesting feels. The zooming speed can be varied. You can also employ a black cardboard with an array of symetrical or asymetrical holes in it and holding it against the lens. You can also exposed with nothing in front of the lens and cover the lens on and off while the exposure completes.<br/> <br/>Now, the object is to get a pattern which has not total chaos but a sense of cohesion. A better balancing of the colors and of course an artistically pleasing result with the least anount of burn out area.<br/> <br/>Since you took what you took I can say that it gives a sense of movement. The abstract qualities often find enough takers to like it, bit some are turned off by the burnt out areas when they become predominant. The image has charm because the overall effect here are diagonals with a vanishing point implied. Keep experimenting and you will be surprised at your output when you center on an idea.<br/> <br/></td>', 'from the critique club: With this piece you have entered the controversial world of the love or hated image. Here we are not going to spend time duscussing composition but rather some of the procedures employed to produce these type of images. Since you as the creator is not even aware of the final shape of such creations it then behooves you to do many takes so that the most pleasing can be selected. It involves many takes and then closing the lens and changing the time. After some experience you will develop a taste for the most appropiate selection and the technique you wish to employ. The variations range from holding camera steady and then suddenly flipping upside down first with equal split of the time and then 2/3 time and then flipping, etc. Another idea is to use a black cardboard and cover half the lens and then either getting the cardbotd out of the way or covering the other half. Another idea is to hold camera steady and then zoom either in out out, both give you interesting feels. The zooming speed can be varied. You can also employ a black cardboard with an array of symetrical or asymetrical holes in it and holding it against the lens. You can also exposed with nothing in front of the lens and cover the lens on and off while the exposure completes. Now, the object is to get a pattern which has not total chaos but a sense of cohesion. A better balancing of the colors and of course an artistically pleasing result with the least anount of burn out area. Since you took what you took I can say that it gives a sense of movement. The abstract qualities often find enough takers to like it, bit some are turned off by the burnt out areas when they become predominant. The image has charm because the overall effect here are diagonals with a vanishing point implied. Keep experimenting and you will be surprised at your output when you center on an idea. ', '2004-08-30 23:09:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(884988, 97306, 25843, '<td valign="top">very nice Neon, wonderful shot :-)</td>', 'very nice Neon, wonderful shot :-)', '2004-08-31 02:50:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(885141, 98498, 25024, '<td valign="top">Fabulous image - well desreved ribbon!</td>', 'Fabulous image - well desreved ribbon!', '2004-08-31 08:20:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(885452, 98083, 1143, '<td valign="top">Hi!<br/>My biggest problem with voting on the neon challenge was the lack of variety. It got a bit boring to see so many pictures of the same thing. This photo isn''t bad per say, but it doesn''t have anything to set it apart from the others. The reflections in the water are pretty and do make me want to find out what''s making them, but the main subject just isn''t interesting. I''m looking closely trying to figure out what made you want to take this picture.<br/>Technically, exposure is good for a night shot. Focus is good although the subject is really too far away for it to matter much. <br/>I''m not really sure how to improve the shot and give it more "wow". I''d focus more on the roof shapes and lights maybe by doing a sort of abstract shot, but most voters have a love/hate relationship with abstract so it probably wouldn''t score better. Maybe taking it earlier in the evening would give the sky some color and help the buildings to stand out so that the overall picture isn''t so dark. Overall, average subject that was shot well but doesn''t hold the viewer''s interest.</td>', 'Hi!My biggest problem with voting on the neon challenge was the lack of variety. It got a bit boring to see so many pictures of the same thing. This photo isn''t bad per say, but it doesn''t have anything to set it apart from the others. The reflections in the water are pretty and do make me want to find out what''s making them, but the main subject just isn''t interesting. I''m looking closely trying to figure out what made you want to take this picture.Technically, exposure is good for a night shot. Focus is good although the subject is really too far away for it to matter much. I''m not really sure how to improve the shot and give it more "wow". I''d focus more on the roof shapes and lights maybe by doing a sort of abstract shot, but most voters have a love/hate relationship with abstract so it probably wouldn''t score better. Maybe taking it earlier in the evening would give the sky some color and help the buildings to stand out so that the overall picture isn''t so dark. Overall, average subject that was shot well but doesn''t hold the viewer''s interest.', '2004-08-31 14:00:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(885454, 98534, 1143, '<td valign="top">Yay! A subject that isn''t as boring as the rest  :)<br/>Just a few minor technical suggestions. What''s the blue line in the background? The crop seems a bit too tight on the sides... maybe leave a bit more space on the left side. Also, need more dof. It''s annoying that most of the creature is blurry. Would like to see at least the front half in focus. This is a scorpion, isn''t it? Doesn''t look like a lobster to me *grin* Nice job coming up with something different from the majority of the boring neon light shots.</td>', 'Yay! A subject that isn''t as boring as the rest  :)Just a few minor technical suggestions. What''s the blue line in the background? The crop seems a bit too tight on the sides... maybe leave a bit more space on the left side. Also, need more dof. It''s annoying that most of the creature is blurry. Would like to see at least the front half in focus. This is a scorpion, isn''t it? Doesn''t look like a lobster to me *grin* Nice job coming up with something different from the majority of the boring neon light shots.', '2004-08-31 14:04:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(886015, 98458, 17126, '<td valign="top">OK, but am I the only one that sees animal shapes in the towels? I thought the buttons were eyes and the towels were a fish, rabbit, and duck, from left to right... I guess it''s just a weird coincidence.</td>', 'OK, but am I the only one that sees animal shapes in the towels? I thought the buttons were eyes and the towels were a fish, rabbit, and duck, from left to right... I guess it''s just a weird coincidence.', '2004-08-31 20:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(892301, 98247, 26332, '<td valign="top">There appears to be a little photo manipulation here but it works well. If not, then you captured just the right lighting. Interesting.</td>', 'There appears to be a little photo manipulation here but it works well. If not, then you captured just the right lighting. Interesting.', '2004-09-04 02:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(892470, 97669, 25024, '<td valign="top">Astounding image. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'Astounding image. Keep up the good work!', '2004-09-04 08:43:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(895299, 98430, 4871, '<td valign="top">Incredible photograph!!! WOW!!! What an amazing place. We''re planning a trip to visit there, but now we''re definitely going to make it a night-time visit. Well done on your ribbon :)</td>', 'Incredible photograph!!! WOW!!! What an amazing place. We''re planning a trip to visit there, but now we''re definitely going to make it a night-time visit. Well done on your ribbon :)', '2004-09-06 09:46:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(895627, 98187, 11793, '<td valign="top">well done for a hand held zoom shot ;}<br/> <br/>the text is crisp in the large version?<br/> <br/></td>', 'well done for a hand held zoom shot ;} the text is crisp in the large version? ', '2004-09-06 12:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(896598, 97600, 10084, '<td valign="top">Beautifully captured composition. A bit more sharpness would definitely help improve the scene. Taking shots of droplet of water is very difficult, but your attempt is worth recreating as this type of shot would be very saleable.<br/> <br/>The contrasting colors are really beautiful and make this very interesting. The colors of the ripples gives a surreal feeling.<br/> <br/>Tiny bit of noise reduction would also help here.This is definitely a great do over shot/recreation shot. If you do please post for everybody to enjoy.</td>', 'Beautifully captured composition. A bit more sharpness would definitely help improve the scene. Taking shots of droplet of water is very difficult, but your attempt is worth recreating as this type of shot would be very saleable. The contrasting colors are really beautiful and make this very interesting. The colors of the ripples gives a surreal feeling. Tiny bit of noise reduction would also help here.This is definitely a great do over shot/recreation shot. If you do please post for everybody to enjoy.', '2004-09-06 23:35:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(903504, 98480, 26464, '<td valign="top">I think this is well-composed.  I like the outer white light with the red.. the tunnel light draws the eye back into the image rather than leading it out. only thing i would''ve liked to see different is a pure white light at the tunnel opening rather than obscured.<br/></td>', 'I think this is well-composed.  I like the outer white light with the red.. the tunnel light draws the eye back into the image rather than leading it out. only thing i would''ve liked to see different is a pure white light at the tunnel opening rather than obscured.', '2004-09-10 14:40:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(907024, 98488, 14043, '<td valign="top">So, am I right in guessing that it didn''t do very well because I over-contrasted it?  (Well and the other issues that I already knew and tried to fix, but couldn''t.)<br/> <br/>Thanks!</td>', 'So, am I right in guessing that it didn''t do very well because I over-contrasted it?  (Well and the other issues that I already knew and tried to fix, but couldn''t.) Thanks!', '2004-09-13 03:33:36.000000', NULL, 0),
